STEP — Collapsible Sidebar

New file:

hospital/js/app-shell.js

Responsibility:

Handle behavior belonging to the common application shell.

Current responsibility:

Collapse and expand the sidebar.

Important line:

sidebar.classList.toggle("collapsed");

classList.toggle() adds the class if it is not present
and removes it if it is already present.

This allows JavaScript to change the UI by changing
a CSS class rather than manually changing many CSS properties.

Relationship:

JavaScript:
    Adds/removes "collapsed"

CSS:
    Defines what "collapsed" means

This is a useful separation of responsibility.

app-shell.js does not decide how the collapsed sidebar
looks.

style.css does that.

Why a new file was created:

The sidebar behavior is now common application-shell
behavior and can be reused by multiple pages.

This is a stronger reason for a separate file than
simply creating files for every small piece of code.


